      "html": "<ul><li>TDS: ~60–100</li><li>pH: ~5.0–7.0</li><li>Temperature: 72–82°F (prefer cooler temperatures, but higher temperatures induce coloration and breeding behaviours)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-ocellata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Currently fed live, frozen and dried foods, including blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-ocellata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Like many of the species in this complex, with the largest bettas, they can be aggressive. It is recommended to keep them in a species-only tank as they can eat anything that fits in their big mouth.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-ocellata-wild-type-bettas",
      "html": "<p>Light brown to tan base body with light blue iridescence on the opercular cheeks and lower jaws, body and tails; females are less iridescent. Fully grown adult males have longer ventral fins and larger bodies.</p>"
    },
